This package provides training guidance and helper scripts for Laya.
Laya is developed by Convai Innovations and its upstream contributors under
the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Upstream repository: https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya
Upstream licence: https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya/blob/fe9a6c35023a7d94102e7feaaeaae8857d9d1b07/LICENSE
Published model: https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya

The helper scripts use Laya's documented Python interfaces and training-row
format. This package does not include the Laya implementation, official
notebook or model weights. Those components are obtained separately and
remain subject to their own applicable licences and notices.

Practice data: the assets/snips folder of the laya-training skill contains a
converted copy of the SNIPS NLU benchmark (2017 custom intent engines) by
Snips, now managed by Sonos, released under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://github.com/sonos/nlu-benchmark
CC0 places no conditions on use. Separately, the publisher's README states
that any publication based on the data must include a full citation to:
Coucke A. et al., "Snips Voice Platform: an embedded Spoken Language
Understanding system for private-by-design voice interfaces." 2018.
https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.10190

